# Cluster development

Before making any change in this repo, read and follow
`.claude/skills/cluster-development/SKILL.md` — the authoritative workflow for
this Proxmox + Ansible + Terraform + k3s/Flux cluster. `CLAUDE.md` and
`AGENTS.md` point at the same skill.

The rules that must hold in every change, restated here because they are the
ones that cost real damage:

- Never push to the default branch; branch plus merge request, always.
- Never commit secrets — host tooling uses references, workloads use
  `ExternalSecret`.
- Flux owns all of `kubernetes/`: no `kubectl apply`, no `helm upgrade`. Preview
  with `task flux:lint`, deploy by merging.
- Kubernetes manifests carry no site literals; `${cluster_...}` substitutions
  come from the `cluster-config` ConfigMap.
- Versions are single-sourced in `ansible/inventories/prod/group_vars/all.yml`,
  followed by `task flux:sync-versions`.
- Ansible roles ship in the weisssrv.infra collection — change them there and
  bump the pin, never in this tree.
- Run `task lint` before opening a merge request.
